 "priorEvidenceFile": "work/investigations/r3-claude/vehbit/Infidel.z3.json",
 "notes": "barge (211) CONFIRMED from Barge Chamber room 115 (infc.log.json): GET IN/ENTER/BOARD BARGE move parent 115->211; GET OUT OF BARGE and STAND UP return 211->115. EXIT is REFUSED in the barge ('You can't go that way.'), SIT ON BARGE 'Bizarre!', CLIMB ON BARGE fails. From other Barge Chamber rooms (116,117,119) 'There's no way to do that from here'; from room 120 GET IN/ENTER BARGE is plain travel to the Center of Barge ROOM 114 (parent = room, not 211). wooden beam (104): every enter verb refused ('Get real. You don't have fly feet.'); STAND ON BEAM over the niches prints 'You are now standing on the beam' but parent stays the room 187 (flag-based, not containment), and GET OFF BEAM there kills the player -> beam is a negative for Enter/Exit.",
 "method": "headless Chromium play.html via drive2.cjs: Input.Inject of ordinary commands only (no VM writes/snapshots). Navigation helpers GOTO/ENSURE only issue ordinary direction commands chosen by BFS over ExitCalibrator.exitsFor (read-only). parent = ZRamReader.objectLinks(mem, WorldModel.lastPayload.playerId).parent before/after each command."
